8 437z"></path></svg> <span>Output Devices</span> </a><a class="custom-nav-node" href="computer-shortcut-keys" title="Computer Shortcut Keys"><svg fill="currentColor" height="1em" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewbox="0 0 512 512" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M256 8C119.043 8 8 119.083 8 256c0 136.997 111.043 248 248 248s248-111.003 248-248C504 119.083 392.957 8 256 8zm0 448c-110.532 0-200-89.431-200-200 0-110.495 89.472-200 200-200 110.491 0 200 89.471 200 200 0 110.53-89.431 200-200 200zm107.244-255.2c0 67.052-72.421 68.084-72.421 92.863V300c0 6.627-5.373 12-12 12h-45.647c-6.627 0-12-5.373-12-12v-8.659c0-35.745 27.1-50.034 47.579-61.516 17.561-9.845 28.324-16.541 28.324-29.579 0-17.246-21.999-28.693-39.784-28.693-23.189 0-33.894 10.977-48.942 29.969-4.057 5.12-11.46 6.071-16.666 2.124l-27.824-21.098c-5.107-3.872-6.251-11.066-2.644-16.363C184.846 131.491 214.94 112 261.794 112c49.071 0 101.45 38.304 101.45 88.8zM298 368c0 23.159-18.841 42-42 42s-42-18.841-42-42 18.841-42 42-42 42 18.841 42 42z"></path></svg> <span>Shortcut Keys</span></a></div></div><h1 class="h1">Computer Fundamentals Tutorial</h1><div style="font-size:14px;margin-top:5px;margin-bottom:5px;color:#6f6e6e"><span>10 Apr 2025</span> | <span><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 2 min read</span></div><p>Computer fundamentals tutorial provides basic and advanced concepts of computer hardware, software, operating systems, peripherals, etc. This tutorial is intended to help you improve and advance your computer skills whether you are a beginner or an experienced professional.</p><img alt="Computer Fundamentals Tutorial" src="https://images.tpointtech.com/computer/images/computer-fundamentals-tutorial.png"><h2 class="h2">What is Computer?</h2><p>Computer is an <em>electronic device</em> that can process information, store data, and carry out tasks. It is derived from the Latin word "computare" which means to calculate. It takes row data as an input, processes it, and then gives result as desired. Similar to a personal assistant, a computer follows instructions to complete tasks effectively. It contains memory that holds memory temporarily through which the computer can quickly access it when needed.</p><p>There are so many key components included in the computer such as <a href="computer-memory">memory</a> <a href="ram">(RAM)</a>, <a href="ssd-vs-hdd">storage (HDD/SSD)</a>, <a href="central-processing-unit">central processing unit (CPU)</a>, <a href="keyboard">keyboard</a>, <a href="mouse">mouse</a> (<a href="input-devices-of-computer">Input devices</a>), <a href="monitor">monitor</a>, <a href="printers">printer</a> (<a href="output-devices-of-computer">output devices</a>), and <a href="peripheral-devices">peripherals</a> (<a href="what-is-usb">USB</a> drives) as well.</p><div class="index"><h2 class="h2">Computer Basics</h2><ul><li><a href="/computer-fundamentals-tutorial">Computer Fundamentals</a></li><li><a href="/what-is-computer">What is Computer?</a></li><li><a href="/advantages-and-disadvantages-of-computer">Advantages and Disadvantages of Computer</a></li><li><a href="/characteristics-of-computer">Characteristics of Computer</a></li><li><a href="/types-of-computer">Types of Computer</a></li></ul><h2 class="h2">Computer History and Generations</h2><ul><li><a href="/history-of-computer">History of Computers</a></li><li><a href="/generation-of-computer">Generations of Computers</a></li><li><a href="/first-generation-of-computer">First Generation of Computer</a></li><li><a href="/second-generation-of-computer">Second Generation of Computer</a></li><li><a href="/third-generation-of-computer">Third Generation of Computer</a></li><li><a href="/fourth-generation-of-computer">Fourth Generation of Computer</a></li><li><a href="/fifth-generation-of-computer">Fifth Generation of Computer</a></li></ul><h2 class="h2">Computer Components</h2><ul><li><a href="/components-of-computer">Components of Computer</a></li><li><a href=